1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
Thank you.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
Thank you.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:29,980
Thank you.

4
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:59,980
Thank you.

5
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:29,980
Thank you.

6
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Don't you think, sir,

7
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:44,000
considering what is happening in the world,

8
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:49,020
in India, in Europe and in America,

9
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:56,060
the general degeneration in literature, in art,

10
00:02:56,060 --> 00:02:59,060
and especially in the culture,

11
00:02:59,060 --> 00:03:00,000
deep culture,

12
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,940
cultural sense, in the sense religion,

13
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:14,940
there is a traditional approach,

14
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:20,040
a mere acceptance of authority, belief,

15
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:25,040
which is not really the religious spirit.

16
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:29,060
Seeing all this, the confusion,

17
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:31,080
the great misery,

18
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:40,060
the sense of infinite sorrow,

19
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:44,000
any observant and most serious people

20
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:52,100
would say that society cannot possibly be changed

21
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:58,120
except only when the individual,

22
00:03:58,120 --> 00:03:59,040
the individual,

23
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:01,040
the human being,

24
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:05,079
really transforms himself radically,

25
00:04:05,079 --> 00:04:11,120
that is, regenerates himself fundamentally.

26
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:17,159
And the responsibility of that depends on the human being,

27
00:04:17,159 --> 00:04:19,659
not on the mass or on the

28
00:04:19,659 --> 00:04:22,159
priest or on a church or a temple

29
00:04:22,159 --> 00:04:24,100
or mosque or whatever it is,

30
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:28,100
but on a human being who is aware

31
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:31,180
of this enormous confusion,

32
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:34,100
politically, religiously, economically,

33
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:37,220
in every direction.

34
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:42,100
There is such misery,

35
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:46,220
such unhappiness.

36
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:49,100
And when you see that,

37
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:56,100
it is a very serious thing

38
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:58,100
to ask oneself,

39
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:04,100
whether a human being like oneself or another,

40
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:08,100
whether he can really deeply undergo

41
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:11,100
a radical transformation.

42
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:17,100
And when that question is put to him,

43
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:20,140
and when he sees his responsibility

44
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:23,100
in relation to the whole,

45
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:27,100
then perhaps we can discuss

46
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:32,100
what relationship has knowledge

47
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:37,100
and time in the transformation of man.

48
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:39,100
I quite follow.

49
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:42,100
We need then to lay some groundwork

50
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:45,100
in order to move into the question itself.

51
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:49,100
Yes, because most people

52
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:52,100
are not concerned with the world at all.

53
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:56,100
Most people are not concerned seriously

54
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:59,100
with the events, with the chaos,

55
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:02,100
with the mess in the world at present.

56
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:05,100
They are only concerned very superficially

57
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:07,100
with the problem of energy,

58
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:11,100
the problem of pollution, and so on,

59
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:13,100
such superficial things.

60
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:16,100
But they are really not deeply concerned

61
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:21,100
with the human mind,

62
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:25,100
the mind that is destroying the world.

63
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:28,100
Yes, yes, I quite follow.

64
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:33,100
What you have said places in a very cardinal way

65
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:36,100
the radical responsibility on the individual as such,

66
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:38,100
if I have understood you correctly.

67
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:40,100
There are no five-year plans

68
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:42,100
that we can expect to help us out.

69
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:46,100
The word individual really is not the correct word

70
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:50,100
because individual, as you know, sir, means

71
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:54,100
undivided, indivisible,

72
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:55,100
in himself.

73
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:58,100
But human beings are totally fragmented,

74
00:06:58,100 --> 00:07:00,100
therefore they are not individuals.

75
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:03,100
They may have a bank account, a name, a house,

76
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:06,100
but they are not really individuals in the sense

77
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:12,100
a total, complete, harmonious whole,

78
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:13,100
unfragmented.

79
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:17,100
That's really what it means to be an individual.

80
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:22,100
Would you say then that to move or make passage,

81
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:25,100
or perhaps a better word simply would be change,

82
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:27,100
since we are not talking about time,

83
00:07:27,100 --> 00:07:31,100
from this fragmented state

84
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:34,100
to one of wholeness,

85
00:07:34,100 --> 00:07:37,100
could be regarded as a change

86
00:07:37,100 --> 00:07:40,100
in the level of the being of the person?

87
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:41,100
Yes.

88
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:42,100
Could we say that?

89
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:43,100
Yes.

90
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:47,100
But you see again the word whole implies

91
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:53,100
not only sanity,

92
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:55,100
health,

93
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:58,100
and also the word whole means holy,

94
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:00,100
h-o-l-y.

95
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:04,100
All that is implied in that one word, whole.

96
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:10,100
And human beings are never whole,

97
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:12,100
they are fragmented,

98
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:14,100
they are contradictory,

99
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:20,100
they are torn apart by various desires.

100
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:24,100
So when we talk of an individual,

101
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:28,100
the individual is really a human being

102
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:33,100
who is totally, completely whole,

103
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:38,100
sane, healthy, and therefore holy.

104
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:44,100
And to bring about such a human being

105
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:47,100
is our responsibility

106
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:50,100
in education, politically, religiously,

107
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:53,100
in every way.

108
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:56,100
And therefore it is the responsibility

109
00:08:56,100 --> 00:09:00,100
of the educator, of everybody,

110
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:03,100
not just myself, my responsibility.

111
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:06,100
It is your responsibility as well as mine,

112
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:08,100
as well as his.

113
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:10,100
It is everyone's responsibility.

114
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:12,100
Absolutely, because we have created

115
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:15,100
this awful mess in the world.

116
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:17,100
But the individual is the one

117
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:18,100
who must make the start.

118
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:20,100
A human being.

119
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,100
Right.

120
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,100
Each human being,

121
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:23,100
whether it is a human being

122
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:24,100
or a politician,

123
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:26,100
or a businessman,

124
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:31,100
or just an ordinary person like me in the street,

125
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:34,100
it is our business as a human being

126
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:39,100
to realise the enormous suffering,

127
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:42,100
misery, confusion there is in the world.

128
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:45,100
And it is our responsibility to change all that.

129
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:46,100
Not the politicians,

130
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:48,100
not the businessmen,

131
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:49,100
not the scientists.

132
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:52,100
It is our responsibility.

133
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:53,100
When we say,

134
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:57,100
it is only our responsibility.

135
00:09:57,100 --> 00:10:01,100
And we have two uses of the word individual now.

136
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:04,100
There is the general use of it,

137
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:07,100
meaning a quantitative measure.

138
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:08,100
Yes.

139
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:11,100
And then this qualitative reference

140
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:15,100
that we have simply needed,

141
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:16,100
it seems to me,

142
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:20,100
to discern as a possibility.

143
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:22,100
I am reminded again

144
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:24,100
of the statement that you made

145
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:26,100
that I quoted earlier,

146
00:10:26,100 --> 00:10:30,100
that it is the responsibility of each human person.

147
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:31,100
Human being, yes.

148
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:32,100
Right.

149
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:33,100
Whether he is in India,

150
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:34,100
or in England,

151
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:35,100
or in America,

152
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:36,100
or wherever he is.

153
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:39,100
So we can't slip out of this by saying,

154
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:41,100
we have created this,

155
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:43,100
therefore we must change it.

156
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:44,100
No, no, no.

157
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:45,100
We get back to,

158
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:47,100
well, if the change is going to start at all,

159
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:49,100
it is going to be with each.

160
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:50,100
Yes, sir.

161
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,100
With each.

162
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:52,100
With each human being.

163
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:58,100
Therefore the question arises from that,

164
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:03,100
does a human being realise,

165
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:05,100
with all seriousness,

166
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:09,100
the...

167
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:13,100
his responsibility

168
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:15,100
not only to himself

169
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:20,100
but to the whole of mankind?

170
00:11:20,100 --> 00:11:21,100
It wouldn't appear

171
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:23,100
so from the way things go on.

172
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:24,100
Obviously not.

173
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:26,100
Each one is concerned with his own little,

174
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:30,100
petty little selfish desires.

175
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:33,100
So,

176
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:37,100
responsibility implies

177
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:40,100
tremendous attention, care,

178
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:42,100
diligence,

179
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:46,100
not negligence as now it is going on.

180
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:50,100
Yes, I do follow that.

181
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:53,100
The word we that we used

182
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:55,100
in relation to each

183
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:59,100
brings about the suggestion of a relationship

184
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:03,100
which perhaps we could

185
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:06,100
pursue here a moment.

186
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:09,100
There seems to be something indivisible,

187
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:11,100
apparently, between

188
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:14,100
what we refer to by each

189
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,100
or the individual person

190
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:19,100
as the usage is usually construed,

191
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:23,100
seems to be an indivisible relation

192
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:25,100
between that

193
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:27,100
and what we call the whole,

194
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:29,100
which the individual doesn't sense.

195
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:32,100
Sir,

196
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:34,100
as you know, I have been

197
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:36,100
all over the world,

198
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:38,100
except behind the Iron Curtain

199
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:40,100
and the bamboo curtain,

200
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:42,100
I've been all over.

201
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:44,100
And I've talked, seen

202
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:47,100
dozens and thousands of people.

203
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:49,100
I've been doing this for fifty years

204
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:52,100
and more.

205
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:54,100
Human beings,

206
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:56,100
wherever they live,

207
00:12:56,100 --> 00:12:59,100
are more or less the same.

208
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:03,100
They have their problems of sorrow,

209
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:05,100
problems of fear,

210
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:08,100
problems of livelihood,

211
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:12,100
problems of personal relationship,

212
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:14,100
problems of survival,

213
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:16,100
overpopulation,

214
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:18,100
and whether this enormous problem

215
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:19,100
of life

216
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:21,100
or the problem of death,

217
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:24,100
it's a common problem to all of us.

218
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:26,100
There is no eastern problem

219
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:29,100
and western problem.

220
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:33,100
The west has its particular civilisation

221
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:36,100
and the east has its own.

222
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:38,100
And human beings

223
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:40,100
are caught in this trap.

224
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:42,100
Yes, I follow that.

225
00:13:42,100 --> 00:13:45,100
And they don't seem to be able

226
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:47,100
to get out of it.

227
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,100
They are going on and on

228
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:52,100
for millennia.

229
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,100
Therefore the question is,

230
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:55,100
how does he bring this about

231
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:59,100
as an each, as a one?

232
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:00,100
The word individual,

233
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:02,100
as you've just described it,

234
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:06,100
seems to me to have a relationship

235
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:09,100
to the word transform in itself.

236
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:11,100
And I'd like to ask you

237
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:16,100
whether you would agree in this.

238
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:17,100
It seems that many persons

239
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:20,100
have the notion that to transform a thing

240
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:22,100
means to change it utterly

241
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:24,100
without any relationship whatsoever

242
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:28,100
to what it is as such.

243
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:30,100
That would seem to ignore

244
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:32,100
that we are talking about a form

245
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:34,100
that undergoes a change,

246
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:36,100
which form itself still abides.

247
00:14:36,100 --> 00:14:38,100
Yes, sir, I understand.

248
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:40,100
Otherwise the change would involve a loss.

249
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:44,100
So are we asking this question, sir,

250
00:14:44,100 --> 00:14:46,100
what place

251
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:49,100
has knowledge

252
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:53,100
in the regeneration of man,

253
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,100
in the transformation of man,

254
00:14:55,100 --> 00:15:01,100
in the fundamental, radical

255
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:03,100
movement in man?

256
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:05,100
What place has knowledge

257
00:15:05,100 --> 00:15:07,100
and therefore time?

258
00:15:07,100 --> 00:15:08,100
Is that what you are asking, sir?

259
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:09,100
Yes, yes I am.

260
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:12,100
Because either we accept

261
00:15:12,100 --> 00:15:15,100
that a change that is a genuine change

262
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:18,100
means the annihilation of what preceded,

263
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:20,100
or we are talking about

264
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:22,100
a total transformation

265
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:24,100
of something that abides.

266
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:25,600
Yes. So let us look

267
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:27,100
at that word for a minute.

268
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:29,100
Good.

269
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:33,100
Revolution,

270
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:36,100
in the ordinary sense of that word,

271
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:39,100
means, doesn't it,

272
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:43,100
not an evolution,

273
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:45,100
a gradual evolution,

274
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:47,100
it is a revolution.

275
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:50,100
No, it doesn't mean that, right, I agree.

276
00:15:50,100 --> 00:15:53,100
A revolution is generally meant

277
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:55,100
if you talk to a communist,

278
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:58,100
he wants to overthrow the government.

279
00:15:58,100 --> 00:16:01,100
If you talk to a bourgeois,

280
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:03,100
he is frightened.

281
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:05,100
If you talk to an intellectual,

282
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:10,100
he has various

283
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:13,100
criticisms about revolution.

284
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:15,100
Now, revolution,

285
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:18,100
is either bloody,

286
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:24,100
or revolution in the psyche.

287
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:27,100
Outward or inner.

288
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:31,100
The outward is the inner.

289
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:33,100
The inner is the outward.

290
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:34,100
There is not the difference

291
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:36,100
between the outer and the inner.

292
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:38,100
They are totally related to each other.

293
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:39,100
Then this goes back

294
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:40,100
to what you mentioned earlier,

295
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:43,100
that there is no division,

296
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:44,100
even though intellectually,

297
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:46,100
you make a distinction here

298
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:48,100
between the I and the we.

299
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:49,100
That's right.

300
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:50,100
Yes, of course.

301
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:55,100
So, when we talk about change,

302
00:16:55,100 --> 00:17:02,100
we mean not the mere bloody revolution,

303
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:04,099
physical revolution,

304
00:17:04,099 --> 00:17:07,099
but rather the revolution

305
00:17:07,099 --> 00:17:11,099
in the make-up of the mind.

306
00:17:11,099 --> 00:17:12,099
Of each person.

307
00:17:12,099 --> 00:17:13,099
Of human beings.

308
00:17:13,099 --> 00:17:14,099
Of human beings.

309
00:17:14,099 --> 00:17:15,099
Right.

310
00:17:15,099 --> 00:17:16,099
The way he thinks,

311
00:17:16,099 --> 00:17:17,099
the way he behaves,

312
00:17:17,099 --> 00:17:19,099
the way he conducts himself,

313
00:17:19,099 --> 00:17:22,099
the way he operates,

314
00:17:22,099 --> 00:17:23,099
he functions,

315
00:17:23,099 --> 00:17:26,099
the whole of that.

316
00:17:26,099 --> 00:17:33,100
Now, whether that psychological revolution,

317
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:35,100
not evolution in the sense,

318
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:36,100
gradualness...

319
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:38,100
No.

320
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:41,100
...what place has knowledge in that?

321
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:43,100
What place has knowledge

322
00:17:43,100 --> 00:17:45,100
in something that occurs...

323
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:49,100
In the regeneration of man,

324
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:51,100
which is the revolution,

325
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:54,100
the inward revolution,

326
00:17:54,100 --> 00:17:55,100
which will affect the outer.

327
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:57,100
Yes, which is not a gradual progress.

328
00:17:57,100 --> 00:17:58,100
No, obviously.

329
00:17:58,100 --> 00:17:59,100
No, right.

330
00:17:59,100 --> 00:18:01,100
The gradual process is endless.

331
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:02,100
Exactly.

332
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:04,100
So we are talking about

333
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:07,100
an instant qualitative change.

334
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:10,100
Again, when you use the word instant,

335
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:12,100
it seems as though,

336
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:15,100
suddenly it is to happen.

337
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:16,100
I don't...

338
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:18,100
That's why I am rather hesitant

339
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:19,100
in using the word instant.

340
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:20,100
Instant.

341
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:22,100
We will go into it in a minute.

342
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:24,100
First of all, sir, let's be clear

343
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:26,100
what you and I are talking about,

344
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:30,100
if we may.

345
00:18:30,100 --> 00:18:34,100
We see, objectively,

346
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:37,100
the appalling mess the world is in.

347
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:38,100
Right?

348
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:39,100
Yes.

349
00:18:39,100 --> 00:18:42,100
The misery, the confusion,

350
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:45,100
the deep sorrow of man.

351
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:47,100
Oh, yes.

352
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:50,100
I can't tell you

353
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:54,100
what I feel when I go round the world,

354
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:56,100
the pettiness, the shallowness,

355
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:59,100
the emptiness of all this,

356
00:18:59,100 --> 00:19:02,100
of the so-called Western civilisation,

357
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:04,100
if I may use that word,

358
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:08,100
into which the Eastern civilisation

359
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:11,100
is being dragged into,

360
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:15,100
and we are just scratching on the surface

361
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:17,100
all the time.

362
00:19:17,100 --> 00:19:22,100
And we think the mere change on the surface,

363
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:25,100
a change in the structure

364
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:28,100
is going to do something enormous to human beings.

365
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:31,100
On the contrary, it has done nothing.

366
00:19:31,100 --> 00:19:34,100
It polishes a little bit here and there,

367
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:36,100
but deeply, fundamentally,

368
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:38,100
it doesn't change man.

369
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:40,100
So, when we are...

370
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:44,100
when we are discussing change,

371
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:47,100
we must be, I think, fairly clear

372
00:19:47,100 --> 00:19:51,100
that we mean the change in the psyche,

373
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:54,100
in the very being of human beings.

374
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:57,100
That is, in the very structure

375
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:59,100
and nature of his thought.

376
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:00,100
A change at the root.

377
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:01,100
At the root.

378
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:02,100
At the root itself.

379
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:03,100
At the root.

380
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:05,100
And therefore, when there is that change,

381
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:09,100
he will naturally bring about a change in society.

382
00:20:09,100 --> 00:20:10,100
It isn't...

383
00:20:10,100 --> 00:20:14,100
Society first, individual or individual first,

384
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:16,100
it is the human change

385
00:20:16,100 --> 00:20:18,100
which will transform the society.

386
00:20:18,100 --> 00:20:21,100
They are not two separate things.

387
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:23,100
Now, I must be very careful

388
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:25,100
that I understand this precisely.

389
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:27,100
Yes.

390
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:30,100
I think I discern now

391
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:33,100
why in the statement you said,

392
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:36,100
which is not dependent on knowledge or time.

393
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:37,100
Yes.

394
00:20:37,100 --> 00:20:39,100
Because when this person changes,

395
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:43,100
this each human being changes.

396
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:46,100
The change that begins in society

397
00:20:46,100 --> 00:20:50,100
is a change that is in a non-temporal relationship

398
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:53,100
with the change in the each human being.

399
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:54,100
Yes, I follow.

400
00:20:54,100 --> 00:20:59,100
After all, human beings have created this society.

401
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:02,100
By their greed, by their anger, by their violence,

402
00:21:02,100 --> 00:21:05,100
by their brutality, by their pettiness,

403
00:21:05,100 --> 00:21:07,100
they have created this society.

404
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:08,100
Precisely.

405
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:12,100
And they think by changing the structure

406
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:14,100
you are going to change the human being.

407
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:16,100
This has been the communist problem,

408
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:19,100
this has been the eternal problem.

409
00:21:19,100 --> 00:21:21,100
That is, change the environment,

410
00:21:21,100 --> 00:21:23,100
then you change man.

411
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:26,100
They have tried that in ten different ways

412
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:27,100
and they haven't done it,

413
00:21:27,100 --> 00:21:29,100
succeeded in changing man.

414
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:34,100
On the contrary, man conquers the environment,

415
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:35,100
the structure.

416
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:37,100
So, if we are clear,

417
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:42,100
if we are clear that the outer is the inner,

418
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:44,100
the inner is the outer,

419
00:21:44,100 --> 00:21:46,100
that there is not the division,

420
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:49,100
the society and the individual,

421
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:55,100
the collective and the separate human being,

422
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:59,100
but the human being is the whole.

423
00:21:59,100 --> 00:22:01,100
He is the society,

424
00:22:01,100 --> 00:22:05,100
he is the separate human individual,

425
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:07,100
he is the fact,

426
00:22:07,100 --> 00:22:12,100
he is the matter which brings about this chaos.

427
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:15,100
Yes, I am following that very closely.

428
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:19,100
Therefore, he is the world and the world is him.

429
00:22:19,100 --> 00:22:20,100
Yes.

430
00:22:20,100 --> 00:22:25,100
Therefore, if he changes, everything changes.

431
00:22:25,100 --> 00:22:28,100
If he doesn't change, nothing changes.

432
00:22:28,100 --> 00:22:29,100
That's right.

433
00:22:29,100 --> 00:22:31,100
I think this is very important

434
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:35,100
because we don't realise, I think,

435
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:42,100
this basic factor that we are the world

436
00:22:42,100 --> 00:22:44,100
and the world is us,

437
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:47,100
that the world isn't something separate from me

438
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:50,100
and me separate from the world.

439
00:22:50,100 --> 00:22:53,100
You are born in a culture,

440
00:22:53,100 --> 00:22:56,100
Christian or Hindu or whatever culture you are born in,

441
00:22:56,100 --> 00:23:00,100
you are the result of that culture.

442
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:05,100
And that culture has produced this world.

443
00:23:05,100 --> 00:23:11,100
The materialistic world of the West,

444
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:14,100
if one can call it,

445
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:19,100
which is spreading all over the world,

446
00:23:19,100 --> 00:23:22,100
destroying their own culture, their own traditions,

447
00:23:22,100 --> 00:23:25,100
everything is being swept aside

448
00:23:25,100 --> 00:23:29,100
in the wake of the Western culture.

449
00:23:29,410 --> 00:23:30,010
嗯

450
00:23:30,018 --> 00:23:35,698
And this culture has produced this human being.

451
00:23:35,718 --> 00:23:41,738
And the human being has created this culture.

452
00:23:41,758 --> 00:23:42,918
Exactly.

453
00:23:42,938 --> 00:23:46,077
He has created the painting, the marvellous cathedrals,

454
00:23:46,098 --> 00:23:50,258
the marvellous technological things,

455
00:23:50,278 --> 00:23:51,998
going to the moon and so on, so on.

456
00:23:52,018 --> 00:23:54,038
His human beings have produced it.

457
00:23:54,058 --> 00:23:55,978
It's the human beings that have created

458
00:23:55,998 --> 00:23:58,958
the rotten society in which we live.

459
00:23:58,958 --> 00:24:01,458
It's the immoral society in which we live,

460
00:24:01,478 --> 00:24:04,298
which human beings have created.

461
00:24:04,318 --> 00:24:05,958
Oh yes, there is no way to know that.

462
00:24:05,978 --> 00:24:10,058
And therefore the world is you, you are the world.

463
00:24:10,078 --> 00:24:13,438
There is no other thing.

464
00:24:13,458 --> 00:24:17,458
If we accept that, if we see that, not intellectually,

465
00:24:17,478 --> 00:24:18,978
but feel it in your heart,

466
00:24:18,978 --> 00:24:20,478
in your mind, in your blood,

467
00:24:20,498 --> 00:24:25,138
that you are that, then the question is,

468
00:24:25,158 --> 00:24:28,758
is it possible for a human being

469
00:24:28,938 --> 00:24:34,518
to transform himself inwardly and therefore outwardly?

470
00:24:34,598 --> 00:24:37,948
I am very concerned to see

471
00:24:37,948 --> 00:24:41,298
this as clearly as I can

472
00:24:41,338 --> 00:24:45,498
in terms of two texts that come to my mind

473
00:24:45,518 --> 00:24:50,938
which, we could say, possess an inner meaning,

474
00:24:50,938 --> 00:24:52,788
and because of this inner outer

475
00:24:52,788 --> 00:24:54,638
thing that we have spoken about

476
00:24:54,658 --> 00:24:58,738
in the divided approach that is made

477
00:24:58,738 --> 00:25:02,338
to scripture. There's a tremendous irony here.

478
00:25:02,358 --> 00:25:09,498
I'm thinking of that, to me, wonderful text

479
00:25:09,518 --> 00:25:16,698
in St. John's Gospel, in the third chapter, which says,

480
00:25:16,718 --> 00:25:18,887
and I'll try to translate

481
00:25:18,887 --> 00:25:21,057
this as the Greek has it,

482
00:25:21,078 --> 00:25:23,718
the one who is doing the

483
00:25:23,718 --> 00:25:26,358
truth is coming to the light.

484
00:25:26,358 --> 00:25:28,678
It isn't that he does the truth

485
00:25:28,678 --> 00:25:30,998
and then later he comes to the light.

486
00:25:31,018 --> 00:25:34,938
And it isn't that we could say from the pulpit,

487
00:25:34,958 --> 00:25:37,118
I will tell you what the truth is.

488
00:25:37,138 --> 00:25:40,598
If you do it, then you'll see the light.

489
00:25:40,618 --> 00:25:43,118
Because we're back again to what you mentioned earlier,

490
00:25:43,138 --> 00:25:49,478
the non-temporal relationship between the action,

491
00:25:49,498 --> 00:25:53,418
which itself is the transformation,

492
00:25:53,438 --> 00:25:56,338
and the marvellous vista

493
00:25:56,358 --> 00:26:00,398
of understanding, which is not an if-then thing,

494
00:26:00,418 --> 00:26:03,118
but is truly concurrent.

495
00:26:03,138 --> 00:26:05,158
And the other one that I thought of,

496
00:26:05,178 --> 00:26:08,298
that I was hoping you might agree in,

497
00:26:08,317 --> 00:26:10,187
is saying the same thing,

498
00:26:10,187 --> 00:26:12,058
so that I understand it well,

499
00:26:12,078 --> 00:26:16,118
in terms of what you've said, is,

500
00:26:16,138 --> 00:26:18,908
and again I'll try to translate

501
00:26:18,908 --> 00:26:21,678
it as literally as I can,

502
00:26:21,698 --> 00:26:26,317
God is love, and the one abiding,

503
00:26:26,358 --> 00:26:29,558
in love,

504
00:26:29,578 --> 00:26:32,458
is abiding in God, and God is abiding in him.

505
00:26:32,477 --> 00:26:34,338
Of course.

506
00:26:34,358 --> 00:26:37,858
I put the ing on all those words

507
00:26:37,877 --> 00:26:42,018
because of the character of the language itself.

508
00:26:42,037 --> 00:26:43,338
It doesn't read to...

509
00:26:43,358 --> 00:26:45,468
one wouldn't want to translate

510
00:26:45,468 --> 00:26:47,578
that for pulpit reading, perhaps,

511
00:26:47,597 --> 00:26:49,377
but that's the real sense of it.

512
00:26:49,398 --> 00:26:51,988
And this inging along gives the

513
00:26:51,988 --> 00:26:54,578
feeling that there's an activity here.

514
00:26:54,597 --> 00:26:56,218
Oh, of course.

515
00:26:56,218 --> 00:26:58,218
That is not bound by temple relations.

516
00:26:58,238 --> 00:27:00,097
It isn't a static state.

517
00:27:00,118 --> 00:27:03,537
It isn't something you intellectually accept it

518
00:27:03,558 --> 00:27:04,798
and leave it like that.

519
00:27:04,817 --> 00:27:07,778
Then it's death, there is nothing in it.

520
00:27:07,798 --> 00:27:09,958
Yes.

521
00:27:09,977 --> 00:27:12,618
That's why...

522
00:27:12,638 --> 00:27:15,438
You see, sir,

523
00:27:15,458 --> 00:27:17,768
we have divided the physical world

524
00:27:17,768 --> 00:27:20,078
as the East and the West.

525
00:27:20,097 --> 00:27:23,778
We have divided religions, Christian religion,

526
00:27:23,798 --> 00:27:26,218
and Hindu, Muslim, Buddhist.

527
00:27:26,238 --> 00:27:30,218
And we have divided the world into nationalities

528
00:27:30,238 --> 00:27:32,218
– the capitalist, the socialist,

529
00:27:32,238 --> 00:27:35,458
the communist and the other people, so on.

530
00:27:35,477 --> 00:27:38,058
We have divided the world,

531
00:27:38,078 --> 00:27:45,458
and we have divided ourselves as Christians, non-Christians.

532
00:27:45,477 --> 00:27:46,218
Yes.

533
00:27:46,237 --> 00:27:50,698
We have divided ourselves into fragments,

534
00:27:50,718 --> 00:27:52,097
opposing each other.

535
00:27:52,117 --> 00:27:55,778
So where there is a division,

536
00:27:55,798 --> 00:27:57,278
there is conflict.

537
00:27:57,298 --> 00:27:59,018
Precisely.

538
00:27:59,038 --> 00:28:02,378
I think that's a basic law.

539
00:28:02,398 --> 00:28:04,177
Where there is a division, there is conflict.

540
00:28:04,198 --> 00:28:06,098
But in terms of that word knowledge,

541
00:28:06,117 --> 00:28:08,818
it appears that people believe, to start with,

542
00:28:08,838 --> 00:28:10,138
that that division is there.

543
00:28:10,158 --> 00:28:12,978
And they operate on that radical belief.

544
00:28:12,998 --> 00:28:16,658
That's why I'm saying it's so important to understand

545
00:28:16,677 --> 00:28:22,098
from the beginning in our talk, in our dialogue,

546
00:28:22,117 --> 00:28:24,958
that the world is not different from me,

547
00:28:24,978 --> 00:28:26,458
and I am the world.

548
00:28:26,478 --> 00:28:33,358
It may sound rather very simplified, simplistic,

549
00:28:33,378 --> 00:28:38,958
but it has got very deep fundamental meaning

550
00:28:38,978 --> 00:28:41,958
if you realise what it means.

551
00:28:41,978 --> 00:28:47,558
Not intellectually, but inwardly, the understanding of it.

552
00:28:47,578 --> 00:28:49,958
Therefore there is no division.

553
00:28:49,978 --> 00:28:52,058
The moment I say to myself,

554
00:28:52,078 --> 00:28:54,238
and I realise that I am the world,

555
00:28:54,238 --> 00:28:55,618
the world is me,

556
00:28:55,638 --> 00:28:57,658
I am not a Christian, or

557
00:28:57,658 --> 00:28:59,678
a Hindu, or a Buddhist, nothing.

558
00:28:59,698 --> 00:29:02,418
I am a human being.

559
00:29:02,438 --> 00:29:07,238
I was just thinking, when you were saying that,

560
00:29:07,258 --> 00:29:11,558
how certain kinds of philosophical analysis

561
00:29:11,578 --> 00:29:13,998
would approach that,

562
00:29:14,018 --> 00:29:16,918
and in terms of the spirit of what you've said,

563
00:29:16,938 --> 00:29:20,238
this really is almost a cosmic joke,

564
00:29:20,258 --> 00:29:22,758
because on the one hand, as you said,

565
00:29:22,758 --> 00:29:24,258
it might sound simplistic.

566
00:29:24,278 --> 00:29:25,718
Some would say it is,

567
00:29:25,738 --> 00:29:27,778
therefore we don't have to pay attention to it.

568
00:29:27,798 --> 00:29:30,898
Others would say, well, it's probably

569
00:29:30,898 --> 00:29:33,998
so much in want of clarity,

570
00:29:34,018 --> 00:29:35,838
even though it's profound,

571
00:29:35,858 --> 00:29:38,938
that it's some kind of mysticism out here.

572
00:29:38,958 --> 00:29:41,758
And we're back and forth with the division again,

573
00:29:41,778 --> 00:29:43,038
as soon as that happens. Again, that's right.

574
00:29:43,058 --> 00:29:44,638
I do follow you.

575
00:29:44,658 --> 00:29:48,138
So, if that is clear,

576
00:29:48,158 --> 00:29:52,738
that there is that human mind

577
00:29:52,758 --> 00:29:56,758
that the human mind has divided the world

578
00:29:56,778 --> 00:30:00,258
in order to find its own security,

579
00:30:00,278 --> 00:30:05,738
which brings about its own insecurity,

580
00:30:05,758 --> 00:30:07,998
when one is aware of that,

581
00:30:08,018 --> 00:30:12,138
then one must inwardly as well as outwardly

582
00:30:12,158 --> 00:30:15,638
deny this division,

583
00:30:15,658 --> 00:30:19,338
as we and they, I and you,

584
00:30:19,358 --> 00:30:22,458
and the Indian and the European,

585
00:30:22,478 --> 00:30:22,738
and the Communist,

586
00:30:22,758 --> 00:30:27,078
you cut at the very root of this division.

587
00:30:27,098 --> 00:30:33,138
Therefore, from that arises the question,

588
00:30:33,158 --> 00:30:36,138
can the human mind,

589
00:30:36,158 --> 00:30:40,778
which has been so conditioned for millennia,

590
00:30:40,798 --> 00:30:42,898
can that human mind,

591
00:30:42,918 --> 00:30:46,518
which has acquired so much knowledge

592
00:30:46,538 --> 00:30:49,038
in so many directions,

593
00:30:49,058 --> 00:30:52,438
can that human mind

594
00:30:52,438 --> 00:31:02,438
change, bring about a regeneration in itself,

595
00:31:02,458 --> 00:31:12,098
and be free to reincarnate now?

596
00:31:12,118 --> 00:31:13,818
Now. Now. Yes.

597
00:31:13,838 --> 00:31:15,198
That is the question.

598
00:31:15,218 --> 00:31:17,318
That's the question.

599
00:31:17,338 --> 00:31:22,118
Exactly. Reincarnate now.

600
00:31:22,118 --> 00:31:23,898
It would appear from what you've said

601
00:31:23,918 --> 00:31:28,018
that one could say that the vast amount

602
00:31:28,038 --> 00:31:33,298
of represented knowledge,

603
00:31:33,318 --> 00:31:36,618
an accretion of centuries,

604
00:31:36,638 --> 00:31:41,238
is a discussion we've been having with ourselves,

605
00:31:41,258 --> 00:31:44,878
regardless of which culture we're speaking about,

606
00:31:44,898 --> 00:31:47,038
as a commentary on this division.

607
00:31:47,058 --> 00:31:48,238
Absolutely.

608
00:31:48,258 --> 00:31:52,098
Without really grasping the division,

609
00:31:52,117 --> 00:31:54,098
it's a division itself.

610
00:31:54,117 --> 00:31:57,598
And of course, since the division is infinitely divisible...

611
00:31:57,617 --> 00:32:00,158
Of course. Why don't you divide? Go on, division.

612
00:32:00,177 --> 00:32:03,197
Exactly. Then we can have tome after tome after tome,

613
00:32:03,217 --> 00:32:04,978
libraries after libraries,

614
00:32:04,998 --> 00:32:07,697
mausoleums of books without end,

615
00:32:07,717 --> 00:32:09,898
because we're continually dividing the division.

616
00:32:09,918 --> 00:32:12,597
That's right. Yes, I follow you.

617
00:32:12,618 --> 00:32:17,858
And you see, that's why

618
00:32:17,878 --> 00:32:21,798
culture is different from civilisation.

619
00:32:21,798 --> 00:32:26,238
Culture implies growth.

620
00:32:26,258 --> 00:32:29,038
Oh yes. Oh yes.

621
00:32:29,058 --> 00:32:36,738
Now, growth in the flowering of goodness.

622
00:32:36,758 --> 00:32:39,038
Lovely phrase. Lovely phrase.

623
00:32:39,058 --> 00:32:42,418
That is culture.

624
00:32:42,438 --> 00:32:43,778
The flowering of goodness. Real culture.

625
00:32:43,798 --> 00:32:46,498
The flowering in goodness. You understand, sir?

626
00:32:46,518 --> 00:32:51,038
Yes. And that doesn't exist.

627
00:32:51,038 --> 00:32:52,478
We have civilisation.

628
00:32:52,498 --> 00:32:54,768
You can travel from India

629
00:32:54,768 --> 00:32:57,038
to America in a few hours.

630
00:32:57,058 --> 00:33:00,158
You have better bathrooms, better this and better that,

631
00:33:00,178 --> 00:33:04,038
and so on, with all the complications that it involves.

632
00:33:04,058 --> 00:33:06,298
That has been the Western culture

633
00:33:06,298 --> 00:33:08,538
which is absorbing the East now.

634
00:33:08,558 --> 00:33:16,717
So, goodness is the very essence of culture.

635
00:33:16,738 --> 00:33:21,038
Religion is the transformation of man.

636
00:33:21,058 --> 00:33:23,217
Not all the belief, churches,

637
00:33:23,238 --> 00:33:29,518
and the idolatry of the Christians or the Hindus.

638
00:33:29,538 --> 00:33:31,597
That's not religion.

639
00:33:31,618 --> 00:33:35,217
So we come back to the point,

640
00:33:35,238 --> 00:33:39,858
if one sees all this in this world, observes it,

641
00:33:39,878 --> 00:33:43,358
not condemn it or justify it, just to observe it,

642
00:33:43,378 --> 00:33:47,837
then from that one asks,

643
00:33:47,858 --> 00:33:51,038
man has collected such enormous information,

644
00:33:51,058 --> 00:33:58,217
knowledge, and has that knowledge changed him into goodness?

645
00:33:58,238 --> 00:34:00,318
You follow, sir? Oh, yes. I follow.

646
00:34:00,337 --> 00:34:04,177
Into a culture that makes him

647
00:34:04,177 --> 00:34:08,018
flower in this beauty of goodness.

648
00:34:08,038 --> 00:34:10,858
It has not. No, it has not.

649
00:34:10,878 --> 00:34:14,638
Therefore it has no meaning.

650
00:34:14,658 --> 00:34:18,538
Excursions into defining goodness is not going to help us.

651
00:34:18,558 --> 00:34:20,797
I mean, you can give explanations

652
00:34:20,818 --> 00:34:23,257
one definition, but that's not...

653
00:34:23,277 --> 00:34:26,558
definitions are not the reality.

654
00:34:26,578 --> 00:34:27,558
No, of course not.

655
00:34:27,578 --> 00:34:29,558
The word isn't the thing.

656
00:34:29,578 --> 00:34:32,898
The description isn't the described.

657
00:34:32,918 --> 00:34:33,918
Precisely.

658
00:34:33,938 --> 00:34:36,697
So, we come back again.

659
00:34:36,717 --> 00:34:39,618
Yes, yes, let's do.

660
00:34:39,638 --> 00:34:42,857
Because I, personally,

661
00:34:42,878 --> 00:34:47,118
I am tremendously concerned with this question.

662
00:34:47,138 --> 00:34:50,697
How to change man?

663
00:34:50,797 --> 00:34:56,438
Because I go to India every year,

664
00:34:56,457 --> 00:34:58,597
for three months or five months,

665
00:34:58,618 --> 00:35:00,418
and I see what is happening there,

666
00:35:00,438 --> 00:35:01,938
and I see what is happening in Europe,

667
00:35:01,957 --> 00:35:05,078
I see what is happening in this country, America,

668
00:35:05,097 --> 00:35:06,998
and it is something...

669
00:35:07,018 --> 00:35:11,078
I can't tell you what shock it gives me

670
00:35:11,097 --> 00:35:13,597
each time I come to these countries.

671
00:35:13,618 --> 00:35:20,318
The degeneration, the superficiality.

672
00:35:20,798 --> 00:35:26,758
The intellectual concepts galore,

673
00:35:26,778 --> 00:35:31,977
without any substance, without any basis,

674
00:35:31,998 --> 00:35:35,638
or a ground in which the beauty of goodness,

675
00:35:35,658 --> 00:35:39,558
of reality can grow.

676
00:35:39,578 --> 00:35:44,477
Now, so, saying all that,

677
00:35:44,498 --> 00:35:50,678
what place has knowledge in the regeneration of man?

678
00:35:50,798 --> 00:35:54,398
That is the basic question.

679
00:35:54,418 --> 00:35:55,898
That's our point of departure.

680
00:35:55,918 --> 00:35:57,678
Departure. Good.

681
00:35:57,698 --> 00:36:00,678
And the knowledge that we have pointed to so far,

682
00:36:00,698 --> 00:36:03,038
that has emerged in our discussion,

683
00:36:03,058 --> 00:36:06,678
is a knowledge which in itself

684
00:36:06,698 --> 00:36:10,798
has no power to effect this transformation.

685
00:36:10,818 --> 00:36:12,977
No, sir, but knowledge has a place.

686
00:36:12,998 --> 00:36:14,238
Yes, I didn't mean that.

687
00:36:14,258 --> 00:36:17,977
I mean what is expected of this knowledge

688
00:36:17,998 --> 00:36:20,758
that we pointed to, that is accumulated in libraries,

689
00:36:20,758 --> 00:36:25,158
is an expectation which it in itself cannot fulfil.

690
00:36:25,178 --> 00:36:27,658
No, no.

691
00:36:27,678 --> 00:36:29,408
I want to... now I must

692
00:36:29,408 --> 00:36:31,138
go back to the word again,

693
00:36:31,158 --> 00:36:32,718
the word knowledge.

694
00:36:32,738 --> 00:36:36,038
What does it mean to know?

695
00:36:36,058 --> 00:36:39,188
Well, I have understood the word

696
00:36:39,188 --> 00:36:42,318
in a strict sense, this way.

697
00:36:42,338 --> 00:36:45,198
Knowledge is the apprehension of what is.

698
00:36:45,218 --> 00:36:47,938
But what passes for knowledge might not be that.

699
00:36:47,958 --> 00:36:50,438
No, what is generally accepted as knowledge,

700
00:36:50,438 --> 00:36:52,837
is experience.

701
00:36:52,857 --> 00:36:54,497
Yes, what is generally accepted.

702
00:36:54,518 --> 00:36:56,198
We'll begin with that, because that's what...

703
00:36:56,217 --> 00:36:58,678
Right, let's begin with what is generally accepted.

704
00:36:58,698 --> 00:37:03,508
Experience, which yields or leaves

705
00:37:03,508 --> 00:37:08,318
a mark which is knowledge.

706
00:37:08,337 --> 00:37:12,237
That accumulated knowledge, whether in the scientific world,

707
00:37:12,258 --> 00:37:16,198
or in the biological world, or in the business world,

708
00:37:16,217 --> 00:37:19,717
or in the world of the mind,

709
00:37:19,737 --> 00:37:20,418
the...

710
00:37:20,438 --> 00:37:25,678
the knowledge being is the known.

711
00:37:25,698 --> 00:37:27,878
The known is the past.

712
00:37:27,898 --> 00:37:32,678
Therefore knowledge is the past.

713
00:37:32,698 --> 00:37:36,198
Knowledge cannot be in the present.

714
00:37:36,217 --> 00:37:40,398
I can use knowledge in the present.

715
00:37:40,418 --> 00:37:41,957
But it's funded from the past.

716
00:37:41,977 --> 00:37:46,878
Yes, but it has its roots in the past.

717
00:37:46,898 --> 00:37:47,878
Yes, I've asked...

718
00:37:47,898 --> 00:37:49,717
Which means... that's very interesting,

719
00:37:49,718 --> 00:37:54,958
because this knowledge which we have acquired,

720
00:37:54,978 --> 00:37:57,478
about everything...

721
00:37:57,498 --> 00:37:58,398
Yes.

722
00:37:58,418 --> 00:38:00,498
You read any... I personally

723
00:38:00,498 --> 00:38:02,578
don't read any of these books,

724
00:38:02,598 --> 00:38:05,578
neither the Bhagavad Gita, Upanishads,

725
00:38:05,598 --> 00:38:08,878
none of the psychological books, nothing.

726
00:38:08,898 --> 00:38:10,898
I'm not a reader.

727
00:38:10,918 --> 00:38:15,578
I have observed tremendously all my life.

728
00:38:15,598 --> 00:38:19,538
Now, knowledge,

729
00:38:19,718 --> 00:38:23,518
has its place.

730
00:38:23,538 --> 00:38:24,738
Oh yes, yes.

731
00:38:24,758 --> 00:38:25,838
Let's be clear.

732
00:38:25,858 --> 00:38:27,658
Oh yes, in the practical order.

733
00:38:27,678 --> 00:38:30,178
Practical, technological,

734
00:38:30,198 --> 00:38:32,098
I must know where I'm going,

735
00:38:32,118 --> 00:38:35,038
physically and so on, so on, so on.

736
00:38:35,058 --> 00:38:39,698
Now, what place has that,

737
00:38:39,718 --> 00:38:43,498
which is human experience as well as scientific knowledge,

738
00:38:43,518 --> 00:38:46,258
what place has that in

739
00:38:46,258 --> 00:38:48,998
changing the quality of a mind

740
00:38:48,998 --> 00:38:55,058
that has become brutal, violent, petty, selfish,

741
00:38:55,078 --> 00:38:58,598
greedy, ambitious and all the rest of that?

742
00:38:58,618 --> 00:39:01,098
What place has knowledge in that?

743
00:39:01,118 --> 00:39:04,038
Well, going back to the statement we began with,

744
00:39:04,058 --> 00:39:06,998
namely that this transformation

745
00:39:06,998 --> 00:39:09,938
is not dependent on knowledge,

746
00:39:09,958 --> 00:39:11,488
then the answer would have to

747
00:39:11,488 --> 00:39:13,018
be it doesn't have a place.

748
00:39:13,038 --> 00:39:17,798
Therefore, let's find out

749
00:39:17,798 --> 00:39:19,977
what are the limits of knowledge.

750
00:39:19,998 --> 00:39:21,618
Yes, yes, of course.

751
00:39:21,638 --> 00:39:26,178
Where is the demarcation,

752
00:39:26,198 --> 00:39:28,818
freedom from the known?

753
00:39:28,837 --> 00:39:31,258
Yes.

754
00:39:31,278 --> 00:39:35,378
Where does that freedom begin?

755
00:39:35,398 --> 00:39:36,857
Good.

756
00:39:36,878 --> 00:39:37,798
You understand? Yes.

757
00:39:37,818 --> 00:39:40,767
Now I know precisely the point at

758
00:39:40,767 --> 00:39:43,717
which we are going to move from.

759
00:39:43,738 --> 00:39:46,418
Where does that freedom begin?

760
00:39:46,438 --> 00:39:47,798
Which is not dependent

761
00:39:47,818 --> 00:39:50,398
on this funded accretion from the past.

762
00:39:50,418 --> 00:39:51,798
That's right.

763
00:39:51,818 --> 00:40:00,798
So, human mind is constructed on knowledge.

764
00:40:00,818 --> 00:40:01,798
Yes.

765
00:40:01,818 --> 00:40:04,298
It has evolved through millennia

766
00:40:04,318 --> 00:40:11,698
on this accretion, on tradition, on knowledge.

767
00:40:11,717 --> 00:40:14,977
Yes. It is there.

768
00:40:14,998 --> 00:40:17,597
And all our actions

769
00:40:17,598 --> 00:40:21,098
are based on that knowledge.

770
00:40:21,118 --> 00:40:23,918
Which by definition must be repetitious.

771
00:40:23,938 --> 00:40:25,358
Obviously. Of course.

772
00:40:25,378 --> 00:40:29,838
And it is repetitious.

773
00:40:29,858 --> 00:40:35,837
So, what place,

774
00:40:35,858 --> 00:40:43,718
what is the beginning of freedom

775
00:40:43,738 --> 00:40:47,597
in relation to knowledge?

776
00:40:47,617 --> 00:40:51,498
May I put it this way, make myself clear?

777
00:40:51,518 --> 00:40:54,097
Yes.

778
00:41:00,498 --> 00:41:04,598
I have experienced something yesterday

779
00:41:04,618 --> 00:41:07,278
that has left a mark.

780
00:41:07,298 --> 00:41:09,998
That is knowledge.

781
00:41:10,018 --> 00:41:15,697
And with that knowledge I meet next experience.

782
00:41:15,717 --> 00:41:17,078
So,

783
00:41:17,098 --> 00:41:23,018
the next experience is translated in terms of the old.

784
00:41:23,038 --> 00:41:27,197
And therefore that experience is never new.

785
00:41:27,218 --> 00:41:29,397
So, in a way, if I understand you correctly,

786
00:41:29,417 --> 00:41:34,498
you are saying that the experience that I had yesterday,

787
00:41:34,518 --> 00:41:36,657
that I recall...

788
00:41:36,677 --> 00:41:37,598
Recollection, yes.

789
00:41:37,618 --> 00:41:42,798
...recollection upon my meeting something new,

790
00:41:42,818 --> 00:41:46,917
that appears to have some relationship to it,

791
00:41:46,918 --> 00:41:49,478
I approach on the basis

792
00:41:49,478 --> 00:41:52,038
of holding my previous knowledge up

793
00:41:52,058 --> 00:41:54,428
as a mirror in which to

794
00:41:54,428 --> 00:41:56,798
determine the nature of this new thing...

795
00:41:56,818 --> 00:41:58,758
Of this, quite. ...that I have confronted.

796
00:41:58,778 --> 00:41:59,918
Quite, quite. Yes.

797
00:41:59,938 --> 00:42:02,298
And this could be a rather crazy mirror.

798
00:42:02,318 --> 00:42:05,398
Generally it is.

799
00:42:05,418 --> 00:42:06,858
So, you see, that is

800
00:42:06,858 --> 00:42:08,298
what I mean. Yes, I follow.

801
00:42:08,318 --> 00:42:11,358
Whether... where is the beginning,

802
00:42:11,378 --> 00:42:16,778
or where is freedom in relation to knowledge?

803
00:42:16,918 --> 00:42:20,508
Or is freedom something other

804
00:42:20,508 --> 00:42:24,098
than the continuity of knowledge?

805
00:42:24,118 --> 00:42:25,598
Must be something other.

806
00:42:25,618 --> 00:42:30,358
Which means, if one goes into it very, very deeply,

807
00:42:30,378 --> 00:42:35,818
it means the ending of knowledge.

808
00:42:35,838 --> 00:42:38,738
Yes.

809
00:42:38,758 --> 00:42:42,158
And what does that mean?

810
00:42:43,858 --> 00:42:45,898
What does it mean

811
00:42:45,918 --> 00:42:46,918
to end knowledge

812
00:42:46,918 --> 00:42:52,678
whereas I have lived entirely on knowledge?

813
00:42:52,698 --> 00:42:54,818
It means that immediately.

814
00:42:54,838 --> 00:43:00,918
I mean, see what is involved in it, sir.

815
00:43:00,938 --> 00:43:04,098
I met you yesterday,

816
00:43:04,118 --> 00:43:08,298
and there is the image of you in my mind,

817
00:43:08,318 --> 00:43:13,478
and that image meets you next day.

818
00:43:13,498 --> 00:43:15,578
Yes. The image meets you.

819
00:43:15,598 --> 00:43:16,698
The image meets you.

820
00:43:16,698 --> 00:43:19,938
The image meets me.

821
00:43:19,958 --> 00:43:24,298
And I have a dozen images, or a hundred images.

822
00:43:24,318 --> 00:43:28,358
So, the image is the knowledge.

823
00:43:28,378 --> 00:43:32,018
The image is the tradition.

824
00:43:32,038 --> 00:43:35,358
The image is the past.

825
00:43:35,378 --> 00:43:41,258
Now, can there be freedom from that?

826
00:43:42,278 --> 00:43:45,358
If this transformation that you speak of is to happen,

827
00:43:45,358 --> 00:43:47,937
is to come to pass, there must be.

828
00:43:47,957 --> 00:43:50,058
Of course. Therefore, how is that?

829
00:43:50,078 --> 00:43:51,917
That's probably... I mean, we can state,

830
00:43:51,937 --> 00:44:00,078
but how is the mind, which thrives, acts, functions

831
00:44:00,098 --> 00:44:06,177
on image, on knowledge, on the known,

832
00:44:06,197 --> 00:44:10,738
how is it to end that?

833
00:44:12,638 --> 00:44:13,878
How am I...

834
00:44:13,897 --> 00:44:14,957
You know, take this very simply.

835
00:44:14,958 --> 00:44:16,358
Take this very simple fact.

836
00:44:16,378 --> 00:44:20,198
You insult me or praise me.

837
00:44:20,218 --> 00:44:25,958
That remains a knowledge.

838
00:44:25,978 --> 00:44:30,718
With that image, with that knowledge, I meet you.

839
00:44:30,738 --> 00:44:32,918
I never meet you.

840
00:44:32,938 --> 00:44:35,038
The image meets you.

841
00:44:35,058 --> 00:44:36,838
Exactly.

842
00:44:36,858 --> 00:44:41,718
Therefore there is no relationship between you and me.

843
00:44:41,738 --> 00:44:44,758
Yes, because between us this has been interposed.

844
00:44:44,758 --> 00:44:45,878
Obviously. Yes.

845
00:44:45,898 --> 00:44:49,998
Therefore, how is that image to end?

846
00:44:50,018 --> 00:44:52,698
Never to register.

847
00:44:52,718 --> 00:44:53,438
You follow?

848
00:44:53,458 --> 00:44:54,328
I can't depend on someone

849
00:44:54,328 --> 00:44:55,198
else to end it for me.

850
00:44:55,218 --> 00:44:57,158
Therefore, what am I to do?

851
00:44:57,178 --> 00:45:00,318
How am I, how is this mind,

852
00:45:00,338 --> 00:45:03,318
which is registering, recording all the time,

853
00:45:03,338 --> 00:45:05,348
the function of the brain

854
00:45:05,348 --> 00:45:07,358
is to record all the time,

855
00:45:07,378 --> 00:45:12,018
how is it to be free of knowledge?

856
00:45:12,038 --> 00:45:14,078
Is it...

857
00:45:14,078 --> 00:45:17,618
When you have done some harm to me,

858
00:45:17,638 --> 00:45:20,318
personally or collectively, whatever way,

859
00:45:20,338 --> 00:45:23,177
you have insulted me, you have flattered me,

860
00:45:23,197 --> 00:45:26,897
how is the brain not to register that?

861
00:45:26,917 --> 00:45:29,057
If it registers, it is already

862
00:45:29,057 --> 00:45:31,197
an image, it is a memory.

863
00:45:31,218 --> 00:45:35,518
And the past then meets the present.

864
00:45:35,538 --> 00:45:37,838
And therefore there is no solution to it.

865
00:45:37,858 --> 00:45:39,638
Exactly.

866
00:45:39,657 --> 00:45:41,958
I was looking up that word the other day

867
00:45:41,978 --> 00:45:43,798
in a very good dictionary,

868
00:45:43,798 --> 00:45:47,917
it is called tradition.

869
00:45:47,938 --> 00:45:49,978
It means, of course, in the ordinary word,

870
00:45:49,998 --> 00:45:53,917
is to give, hand over, give a cross.

871
00:45:53,938 --> 00:45:57,198
But it also has another peculiar meaning,

872
00:45:57,218 --> 00:46:01,858
not peculiar, from the same word, betrayal.

873
00:46:01,878 --> 00:46:05,738
Oh yes, traduce. Traduce.

874
00:46:05,758 --> 00:46:09,318
And in discussing in India this came out,

875
00:46:09,338 --> 00:46:13,038
betrayal of the present.

876
00:46:13,038 --> 00:46:19,298
In the living tradition, I betray the present.

877
00:46:19,318 --> 00:46:20,798
Yes, I do see that.

878
00:46:20,818 --> 00:46:25,558
Which is, knowledge betrays the present.

879
00:46:25,578 --> 00:46:28,157
Which is, in fact, a self-betrayal.

880
00:46:28,178 --> 00:46:29,358
That's right. Yes.

881
00:46:29,378 --> 00:46:37,798
So, how is the mind, which functions on knowledge,

882
00:46:37,818 --> 00:46:42,958
how is the brain, which is recording all the time,

883
00:46:42,958 --> 00:46:51,518
to see the importance of recording,

884
00:46:51,538 --> 00:46:56,918
and not let it move in any other direction?

885
00:46:56,938 --> 00:46:58,828
That is, sir, let me

886
00:46:58,828 --> 00:47:00,718
put it this way, very simply,

887
00:47:00,738 --> 00:47:05,758
you insult me, you hurt me,

888
00:47:05,778 --> 00:47:10,198
by word, gesture, by an actual act.

889
00:47:10,218 --> 00:47:12,898
That leaves a mark,

890
00:47:12,898 --> 00:47:17,418
a mark on the brain, which is memory.

891
00:47:17,438 --> 00:47:18,378
Yes.

892
00:47:18,398 --> 00:47:22,398
That memory is knowledge.

893
00:47:22,418 --> 00:47:25,758
That knowledge is going to interfere

894
00:47:25,778 --> 00:47:28,878
in my meeting you next time.

895
00:47:28,898 --> 00:47:30,218
Obviously.

896
00:47:30,238 --> 00:47:34,418
Now, how is the brain, and also the mind,

897
00:47:34,438 --> 00:47:38,618
how is the brain to

898
00:47:38,618 --> 00:47:42,798
record and not let it interfere

899
00:47:42,798 --> 00:47:44,518
with the present?

900
00:47:44,538 --> 00:47:46,417
Well, the person must, it seems to me,

901
00:47:46,438 --> 00:47:47,917
take pains to negate.

902
00:47:47,938 --> 00:47:49,798
No, no, see what is implied.

903
00:47:49,818 --> 00:47:52,397
I know, but see how am I to negate it?

904
00:47:52,417 --> 00:47:58,018
How is the brain, whose function is to record,

905
00:47:58,038 --> 00:48:01,038
like a computer, it's recording.

906
00:48:01,058 --> 00:48:05,478
I didn't mean to suggest that it negates the recording,

907
00:48:05,498 --> 00:48:10,038
but it's the association, the translation of the recording

908
00:48:10,058 --> 00:48:12,118
into an emotional complex.

909
00:48:12,118 --> 00:48:13,417
That's just the point.

910
00:48:13,437 --> 00:48:20,598
How is it to end this emotional response

911
00:48:20,618 --> 00:48:23,378
when I meet you next

912
00:48:23,378 --> 00:48:26,138
time, you who have hurt me?

913
00:48:26,157 --> 00:48:27,358
That's the problem.

914
00:48:27,378 --> 00:48:30,677
That's the place from which we, in the practical order,

915
00:48:30,697 --> 00:48:35,098
in our relation to ourselves, must then begin.

916
00:48:35,118 --> 00:48:38,758
Yes. Exactly.

917
00:48:38,778 --> 00:48:42,118
There is an aspect of this,

918
00:48:42,138 --> 00:48:44,977
that interests me very much,

919
00:48:44,998 --> 00:48:47,558
in terms of the relation

920
00:48:47,558 --> 00:48:50,118
between the theoretical and the practical.

921
00:48:50,138 --> 00:48:55,618
Sir, to me theory has no reality.

922
00:48:55,638 --> 00:48:59,338
Well, let me put it this way.

923
00:48:59,358 --> 00:49:03,118
Theories have no importance to

924
00:49:03,118 --> 00:49:06,878
a man who is actually living.

925
00:49:06,897 --> 00:49:11,118
May I say what I mean by theory?

926
00:49:11,138 --> 00:49:13,748
I don't think I mean what

927
00:49:13,748 --> 00:49:16,358
you think I mean by it.

928
00:49:16,378 --> 00:49:18,198
I mean theory in the

929
00:49:18,198 --> 00:49:20,018
sense of the Greek word theoria,

930
00:49:20,038 --> 00:49:24,397
spectacle, what is out there that I see.

931
00:49:24,417 --> 00:49:26,397
And the word is therefore very closely related

932
00:49:26,417 --> 00:49:29,197
to what you've been talking about in terms of knowledge.

933
00:49:29,217 --> 00:49:31,607
And yet it is the

934
00:49:31,607 --> 00:49:33,998
case that if we see something,

935
00:49:34,018 --> 00:49:41,058
that something is registered to us in the mind,

936
00:49:41,118 --> 00:49:44,697
in terms of a likeness of it,

937
00:49:44,717 --> 00:49:47,007
otherwise we should have to become

938
00:49:47,007 --> 00:49:49,298
it in order to receive it,

939
00:49:49,318 --> 00:49:52,538
which in the material order would annihilate us.

940
00:49:52,558 --> 00:49:55,697
It seems to me, if I followed you correctly,

941
00:49:55,717 --> 00:50:00,498
that there is a profound confusion in one's relationship

942
00:50:00,518 --> 00:50:03,798
to that necessity for the finite being,

943
00:50:03,818 --> 00:50:06,758
and what he makes of it.

944
00:50:06,778 --> 00:50:10,498
And insofar as he's making the wrong thing of it,

945
00:50:10,498 --> 00:50:10,998
Right.

946
00:50:10,998 --> 00:50:12,618
he is in desperate trouble,

947
00:50:12,638 --> 00:50:16,618
and can only go on repeating himself,

948
00:50:16,638 --> 00:50:21,818
and in such a repetition increasing despair.

949
00:50:21,838 --> 00:50:25,078
Have I distinguished this correctly?

950
00:50:25,098 --> 00:50:27,678
You see,

951
00:50:31,718 --> 00:50:37,238
religion is based on tradition.

952
00:50:37,258 --> 00:50:40,098
Religion is vast propaganda,

953
00:50:40,118 --> 00:50:40,998
as it is now.

954
00:50:41,018 --> 00:50:45,558
In India, here, anywhere, propaganda

955
00:50:45,578 --> 00:50:52,678
of theories, of beliefs, of idolatry, worship,

956
00:50:52,698 --> 00:51:01,178
essentially based on the acceptance of a theory.

957
00:51:01,198 --> 00:51:03,098
Yes, yes.

958
00:51:03,118 --> 00:51:07,758
Essentially based on an idea.

959
00:51:07,778 --> 00:51:10,098
A statement, a postulate.

960
00:51:10,118 --> 00:51:13,038
I mean, they are ideas put out by thought.

961
00:51:13,058 --> 00:51:16,038
Right.

962
00:51:16,058 --> 00:51:20,038
And obviously that's not religion.

963
00:51:23,998 --> 00:51:29,768
So, religion as it exists now

964
00:51:29,768 --> 00:51:35,538
is the very denial of truth.

965
00:51:35,558 --> 00:51:38,738
Yes, yes, I'm sure I understand you.

966
00:51:38,758 --> 00:51:39,858
Mm-hm.

967
00:51:40,098 --> 00:51:48,318
And if a man, like me, wants to find out,

968
00:51:48,338 --> 00:51:50,278
discover what the truth is,

969
00:51:50,298 --> 00:51:53,578
he must deny the whole

970
00:51:53,578 --> 00:51:56,858
structure of religion as it is.

971
00:51:56,878 --> 00:51:58,717
Mm-hm.

972
00:51:58,738 --> 00:52:06,118
Which is idolatry, propaganda, fear, division,

973
00:52:06,138 --> 00:52:10,018
you're Christian, I'm Indian, all that nonsense.

974
00:52:10,018 --> 00:52:11,018
Right.

975
00:52:11,038 --> 00:52:16,518
And be a light to oneself.

976
00:52:16,538 --> 00:52:20,618
Not in the vain sense of that word, or light,

977
00:52:20,638 --> 00:52:25,418
because in darkness, the world is in darkness.

978
00:52:25,438 --> 00:52:29,938
And a human being that has to transform himself

979
00:52:29,958 --> 00:52:34,038
has to be a light to himself.

980
00:52:34,058 --> 00:52:38,478
And light is not lit by somebody else.

981
00:52:38,498 --> 00:52:39,918
So there's a point at which,

982
00:52:39,918 --> 00:52:43,018
he must stop repeating himself.

983
00:52:43,038 --> 00:52:43,738
Ah!

984
00:52:43,758 --> 00:52:45,738
Is that correct? Correct, sir.

985
00:52:45,758 --> 00:52:48,748
In a sense, we could

986
00:52:48,748 --> 00:52:51,738
use the analogy perhaps from surgery.

987
00:52:51,758 --> 00:52:56,338
Something that has been continuous is now cut.

988
00:52:56,358 --> 00:52:57,158
Yes.

989
00:52:57,178 --> 00:53:00,478
And cut radically.

990
00:53:00,498 --> 00:53:04,018
Not just fooled around, but really cut.

991
00:53:04,038 --> 00:53:06,678
Sir, we haven't time to fool around any more.

992
00:53:06,698 --> 00:53:09,678
Exactly. The house is on fire.

993
00:53:09,918 --> 00:53:12,978
At least I feel this enormously,

994
00:53:12,998 --> 00:53:16,138
that things are coming to such a pass,

995
00:53:16,158 --> 00:53:18,938
we must do something, each human being.

996
00:53:18,958 --> 00:53:22,018
Not in terms of better houses, better security,

997
00:53:22,038 --> 00:53:23,978
more this and that,

998
00:53:23,998 --> 00:53:30,138
but basically to regenerate himself.

999
00:53:30,158 --> 00:53:35,018
But if the person believes

1000
00:53:35,038 --> 00:53:39,798
that in cutting himself from this,

1001
00:53:39,798 --> 00:53:44,417
that he is a Christian, that he is killing himself,

1002
00:53:44,438 --> 00:53:46,518
then he is going to resist that idea, isn't he?

1003
00:53:46,538 --> 00:53:47,578
Of course, of course.

1004
00:53:47,598 --> 00:53:52,678
Therefore he has to understand

1005
00:53:52,698 --> 00:53:56,478
what his mind has created.

1006
00:53:56,498 --> 00:53:59,818
Therefore he has to understand himself.

1007
00:53:59,838 --> 00:54:01,498
So he starts observing.

1008
00:54:01,518 --> 00:54:03,098
Himself. Himself.

1009
00:54:03,118 --> 00:54:05,798
Which is the world. Yes.

1010
00:54:05,818 --> 00:54:08,278
Not learning five languages to be able to construe...

1011
00:54:08,298 --> 00:54:09,438
Ah, for God's sake, that's all I know.

1012
00:54:09,438 --> 00:54:11,038
No, no. Yes.

1013
00:54:11,058 --> 00:54:13,898
Or going to schools where you learn sensitivity

1014
00:54:13,918 --> 00:54:16,618
and all that rubbish.

1015
00:54:16,638 --> 00:54:20,298
The point that you are making, it seems to me,

1016
00:54:20,318 --> 00:54:25,758
is made also by the great Danish thinker, Kierkegaard,

1017
00:54:25,778 --> 00:54:31,398
who lived a very trying life in his own community,

1018
00:54:31,418 --> 00:54:34,178
because he was asking them, it seems to me,

1019
00:54:34,198 --> 00:54:36,998
to undertake what you are saying.

1020
00:54:37,018 --> 00:54:39,438
He was saying, look, if I go to seminary,

1021
00:54:39,458 --> 00:54:42,718
and I try to understand what Christianity is

1022
00:54:42,738 --> 00:54:44,878
by studying at my desk,

1023
00:54:44,898 --> 00:54:48,198
then what I am doing is appropriating something here,

1024
00:54:48,218 --> 00:54:50,328
but then when do I know

1025
00:54:50,328 --> 00:54:52,438
when I have appropriated it fully?

1026
00:54:52,458 --> 00:54:54,198
I shall never know that point,

1027
00:54:54,218 --> 00:54:56,318
therefore I shall forever appropriate it

1028
00:54:56,338 --> 00:55:00,558
and never do anything about it as such.

1029
00:55:00,578 --> 00:55:05,818
As a subject, the person who must risk the deed,

1030
00:55:05,838 --> 00:55:08,718
not the utterance of what someone has said before.

1031
00:55:08,738 --> 00:55:09,138
I don't know, of course.

1032
00:55:09,138 --> 00:55:11,167
So not simply thinking through

1033
00:55:11,167 --> 00:55:13,197
what someone has thought before,

1034
00:55:13,217 --> 00:55:17,018
but actually embodying the meaning

1035
00:55:17,038 --> 00:55:20,197
through the observation of myself in relation to that.

1036
00:55:20,217 --> 00:55:20,897
Quite, quite.

1037
00:55:20,917 --> 00:55:23,517
And that has always seemed

1038
00:55:23,517 --> 00:55:26,118
to me a very profound insight.

1039
00:55:26,138 --> 00:55:28,378
But one of the ironies of that is, of course,

1040
00:55:28,397 --> 00:55:34,477
in the academy we have an endless proliferation of studies

1041
00:55:34,497 --> 00:55:36,778
in which scholars have learned Danish

1042
00:55:36,798 --> 00:55:38,437
in order to understand Kierkegaard.

1043
00:55:38,457 --> 00:55:38,917
Oh, well.

1044
00:55:38,918 --> 00:55:43,978
And what they are doing is, to a large extent,

1045
00:55:43,998 --> 00:55:46,238
if I haven't misjudged the spirit

1046
00:55:46,238 --> 00:55:48,478
of much that I have read,

1047
00:55:48,498 --> 00:55:52,328
is simply perpetuate the very

1048
00:55:52,328 --> 00:55:56,158
thing he said should be cut.

1049
00:55:56,178 --> 00:56:00,418
I do have this very strong feeling that

1050
00:56:00,438 --> 00:56:03,538
profound change would take place in the academy,

1051
00:56:03,558 --> 00:56:05,198
of which you know I am a member.

1052
00:56:05,218 --> 00:56:08,218
A member, quite.

1053
00:56:08,218 --> 00:56:13,098
And the teacher were not only

1054
00:56:13,098 --> 00:56:17,978
to grasp this that you have said,

1055
00:56:17,998 --> 00:56:21,478
but take the risk of acting on it,

1056
00:56:21,498 --> 00:56:23,268
since if it isn't acted on,

1057
00:56:23,268 --> 00:56:25,038
if I have understood you correctly,

1058
00:56:25,058 --> 00:56:27,238
we are back again where we were.

1059
00:56:27,258 --> 00:56:29,498
We have toyed with the

1060
00:56:29,498 --> 00:56:31,738
idea of being valiant and courageous,

1061
00:56:31,758 --> 00:56:33,108
but then we have to think

1062
00:56:33,108 --> 00:56:34,458
about what is involved before we do,

1063
00:56:34,478 --> 00:56:35,478
and then we don't do.

1064
00:56:35,498 --> 00:56:36,138
Quite, quite.

1065
00:56:36,158 --> 00:56:36,978
We think and don't do.

1066
00:56:36,998 --> 00:56:37,518
Therefore, sir,

1067
00:56:37,518 --> 00:56:37,538
therefore, sir,

1068
00:56:37,538 --> 00:56:40,978
the word is not the thing.

1069
00:56:40,998 --> 00:56:43,778
The description is not the described.

1070
00:56:43,798 --> 00:56:46,538
And if you are not concerned with the description,

1071
00:56:46,558 --> 00:56:50,478
but only the thing, what is,

1072
00:56:50,498 --> 00:56:52,098
then we have to do something.

1073
00:56:52,118 --> 00:56:56,458
When you are confronted with what is, you act.

1074
00:56:56,478 --> 00:56:59,378
But when you are concerned with theories and speculations

1075
00:56:59,397 --> 00:57:02,138
and beliefs, you never act.

1076
00:57:02,157 --> 00:57:04,058
So there isn't any hope for this transformation,

1077
00:57:04,078 --> 00:57:05,818
if I have understood you correctly,

1078
00:57:05,838 --> 00:57:06,838
if I should think tomorrow,

1079
00:57:06,858 --> 00:57:07,078
if I should think tomorrow,

1080
00:57:07,078 --> 00:57:07,138
if I should think tomorrow,

1081
00:57:07,157 --> 00:57:07,518
if I should think tomorrow,

1082
00:57:07,558 --> 00:57:10,438
I will never be myself.

1083
00:57:10,458 --> 00:57:12,338
That just sounds marvellous.

1084
00:57:12,358 --> 00:57:14,698
I am the world and the world is me,

1085
00:57:14,718 --> 00:57:16,778
while I go on thinking

1086
00:57:16,778 --> 00:57:18,838
that the description is the described.

1087
00:57:18,858 --> 00:57:20,238
There is no hope.

1088
00:57:20,258 --> 00:57:22,998
So we are speaking about a disease over here,

1089
00:57:23,018 --> 00:57:24,458
and we are speaking about something

1090
00:57:24,478 --> 00:57:28,218
that has been stated as the case.

1091
00:57:28,238 --> 00:57:29,608
And if I take what

1092
00:57:29,608 --> 00:57:30,978
has been stated as the case,

1093
00:57:30,998 --> 00:57:33,338
as the case,

1094
00:57:33,358 --> 00:57:36,318
then I am thinking the description is the described.

1095
00:57:36,338 --> 00:57:36,778
Of course.

1096
00:57:36,798 --> 00:57:40,538
It is like a man who is hungry.

1097
00:57:40,558 --> 00:57:43,197
Any amount of description of the right kind of food

1098
00:57:43,217 --> 00:57:45,938
and the beauty of the food will never satisfy him.

1099
00:57:45,958 --> 00:57:50,257
He is hungry, he wants food.

1100
00:57:50,278 --> 00:57:58,257
So all this implies, doesn't it, sir, several things.

1101
00:57:58,278 --> 00:58:02,578
First, can there be freedom from knowledge?

1102
00:58:02,598 --> 00:58:06,398
And knowledge has its place.

1103
00:58:06,398 --> 00:58:07,718
Yes.

1104
00:58:07,738 --> 00:58:16,518
Can there be freedom from the tradition as knowledge?

1105
00:58:16,538 --> 00:58:19,898
From the tradition as knowledge, yes.

1106
00:58:19,918 --> 00:58:26,098
Can there be freedom from this separative outlook,

1107
00:58:26,118 --> 00:58:29,178
me and you, we and they,

1108
00:58:29,198 --> 00:58:32,598
Christians and all this divisive

1109
00:58:32,598 --> 00:58:35,998
attitude or activity in life?

1110
00:58:35,998 --> 00:58:40,118
Those are the problems we have to...

1111
00:58:40,138 --> 00:58:42,518
That is what we must attend

1112
00:58:42,518 --> 00:58:44,898
to as we move through our dialogues.

1113
00:58:44,918 --> 00:58:52,718
So first, can the mind be free from the known?

1114
00:58:52,738 --> 00:58:55,378
I mean, not verbally, but actually.

1115
00:58:55,398 --> 00:58:57,378
But actually, yes.

1116
00:58:57,378 --> 00:58:59,758
I can speculate about what is freedom,

1117
00:58:59,778 --> 00:59:00,758
what is all the rest of it,

1118
00:59:00,778 --> 00:59:05,878
but see the necessity, the importance,

1119
00:59:05,878 --> 00:59:08,478
that there must be freedom from the known.

1120
00:59:08,498 --> 00:59:10,638
Otherwise life becomes repetitive,

1121
00:59:10,658 --> 00:59:15,978
continuous superficial scratching.

1122
00:59:15,998 --> 00:59:18,058
It has no meaning. Of course.

1123
00:59:18,078 --> 00:59:21,118
In our next conversation together,

1124
00:59:21,138 --> 00:59:23,258
I hope we can begin

1125
00:59:23,258 --> 00:59:25,378
where we have just left off.

